        "vizConfig": {
          "group": "text",
          "kind": "VizConfig",
          "spec": {
            "fieldConfig": {
              "defaults": {},
              "overrides": []
            },
            "options": {
              "mode": "markdown",
              "content": "### How to read this dashboard\n\n**Latest call per ticker** is today's actionable view: what the model currently says about everything you hold or watch, strongest calls first (BUY/SELL before WATCH/HOLD).\n\n- **ticker hit rate %** — how often *this ticker's* past calls were right at 30 days: CORRECT ÷ (CORRECT + INCORRECT), neutral outcomes excluded. Trust high-confidence calls on high-hit-rate tickers more.\n- **graded calls** — the sample behind that hit rate; below ~10 it's noise.\n\n**Symbol click-through:** each symbol in the table links to the *Ticker deep dive* dashboard pre-filtered to that ticker. One-time setup: after importing, edit the link's URL and replace `DEEP_DIVE_UID` with the deep-dive dashboard's uid from your Grafana (the segment after `/d/` in its URL) — schema-v2 exports carry no uid, so it can't ship pre-wired.\n\n**Hit rate over time** shows whether accuracy is improving week over week (bars = how many graded calls each week; thin bars mean a noisy percentage). It follows the time picker; the table above always shows the latest run.\n\n**Horizon:** all hit rates are graded at the **30-day** horizon — these are long-term calls (≥1 month, up to a year), not weekly trades. 90d and 1y grading accumulates in the background.",
              "code": {
                "language": "plaintext",
                "showLineNumbers": false,
                "showMiniMap": false
              }
            }
          }
        }
